---
title: Thai Steak Salad Lettuce Wraps with Peanut Sauce
servings: 4
course: Main
locale: en
difficulty: Medium
cuisine: Thai
---

= Cook Steak =

Season the @sirloin steak{700%g}(room temperature) with @salt and @pepper. In a #large frying pan{} heat some @oil over high heat until smoking. Cook the steaks for 2 to ~{3%minutes} on each side, depending on thickness, until medium-rare.

Remove the steaks from the pan and set aside to rest for ~{10%minutes}, then slice thinly.

= Peanut Sauce =

Put the @smooth peanut butter{250%g}, @sriracha or chilli sauce{2%tsp}, @apple cider vinegar{1%tbsp}, @light soy sauce{2%tbsp}, and @honey{1%tsp} into a small bowl. Whisk together until smooth. Thin with @boiling water{5%tbsp} to desired consistency; less water for a thicker dip, more water for a thinner sauce.

= Steak Dressing =

Place the dressing ingredients (@light soy sauce{2%tbsp}, @fish sauce{1%tbsp}, @lime juice{2%tbsp}, and @sweet chilli sauce{2%tbsp}) in a screw-top jar and shake well to combine.

Combine the sliced steak and julienned vegetables in a bowl. Pour over the dressing and toss well to combine and coat.

= Serve =

Fill @lettuce{1}(suitable for wraps) leaf cups with steak and vegetables (@carrot{1%large}(julienned), @red pepper{1%large}(julienned), and @spring onions{3}(thinly sliced)) and scatter with @unsalted roast peanuts{65%g}(chopped) and @chives or coriander{}(snipped). Serve with peanut sauce on the side.